Z||000000||Neverfinished||05-24-2001||06:10 PM||||Does anyone here believe that the US did land on the moon or is it all a big hoax?<BR>I don't think they did at all and it was all a big scam to boost morale in the US and to prove that russians that they suck, which is not completely true.<BR>Please, anyone with an argument on either side use this post to sway my stance on the subject.<P>------------------<BR>To Be Old And Wise, You First Must Be Young And Stupid.-----------------<BR>It's not a waste of time... If you are wasted at the time<p>[This message has been edited by Neverfinished (edited 05-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||JSocha||05-24-2001||06:20 PM||||There was an engineer, Space scienctist, or something like that (Carl Sagen ???) (was on Discovery or the Learning Channel) that somehow had shown that with the technology back then that it would have been virtually impossible to make it through the radiation belt that apparently surrounds us, the Earth without killing the astronaughts.<P>My question is, if we did, how come we never went back?<P>Ken W...got any thoughts on this!<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||05-24-2001||06:56 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JSocha:<BR><B>...My question is, if we did, how come we never went back?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>We did go back. Several times. Even brought a car with us!<BR>I was 12 when the US landed on the moon. I still remember watching it on television. <BR>I am thoroughly convinced that it was authentic. <BR>If for no other reason than the television technology that existed then was too primative to have faked it. <BR>Why didn't we keep going? <BR>Once we had landed on the moon, the next likely target was Mars. <BR>That would have been much more difficult than a lunar landing. <BR>The death blow to manned exploration was the explosion on Apollo 13. The public was getting complacent, anyway. Losing interest. Once apollo 13 happened, it became politically unfashionable to continue. <BR>Viet Nam and Watergate were taking center stage. As for the moon, we had "been there. done that." <BR>NASA funding was drastically reduced.<BR>BTW... I had an instructor in school that had been a part of the Apollo program, at NASA. Reduced to teaching microwave theory at the community college I attended. <BR>Boy, was he pissed at the world!  <P><BR>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 black Formula<BR>88 Duke coupe <BR>88 "wadded up" Formula (parts car)<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 05-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||MotherGoose||05-24-2001||07:22 PM||||We did go back, Apollo 12.  After Apollo 13 they tried to re-engineer the craft so the same thing would not happen again.  However at the same time Vietnam became a problem with the public and a lot of NASA funding went to the DOD to try and win a losing war.  Then the gas crisis, then the shuttle.  The other reason is...we know what's there, and it's not that important, besides to our planets tidal patterns.<P>As for the radiation belt.  The radiation suit has been around since the early 50's.  The suit isn't perfect, but it is only a few millimeters thick.  The capsule was a lot thicker and did the job fine.<P>The most convincing thing is when John Glenn is running on the surface.  There is no pillow of dust when he lands.  That means there was no air pressure to push it up.  You can't do that here.<P>Sorry we were there||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||05-24-2001||07:42 PM||||all the return (?) trips were also back 30 years ago. why havent we gone back since. There were lots of convincing arguments for the conspiracy of not really going. Like obvious faked photos. Flag blowing where theres no atmoshpere. Clear pictures taken in shadows, where there is no air to diffuse light, its either light or dark, no in between. Tons of other stuff. Personally I think it was faked to show we were superior to russians, otherwise wed be back n forth to the moon like the space shuttle.||||reg||1
