Z||000011||JohnnyK||05-25-2001||02:15 AM||||If you remember back, I did a lot of research on this subject. We DID go. It is all easily proven. The guy who came up with the conspiracy had a conversation with Nasa, and he was made a fool of. They practiced for hours with the cameras before they left, and landing craft DID make an impression. The shadows that were "faked" were just due to idiots not realizing that shadows aim different and are longer/shorter when you are on a hill (which they clearly are in all the pictures). The flag was rippling because 1, I don't think it was normal flag material, and the most important thing, is that it wasn't a normal flag pole (It was an L shape, upside down, so the flag hung from 2 sides, if that makes any sense). Anyways, I could go on and on. It's pretty stupid now that I've done all the research to think we've never landed on the moon. And also very inconsiderate considering the people that died during the missions.||||reg||1
