Z||000033||Fiero5||05-25-2001||10:40 PM||||"Did anyone see the TV show on this subject?<BR>I wanted to get the book that it was based on or even a video of the show but I can't find anything."<P>Actually, I remember seeing a pretty cool movie back in the late 70's I think that starred among others someone who is seen a little differently today than he was back then. <BR>This "actor" who I will reveal in a moment played one of three astronauts who were going to Mars. At the last minute, the big wigs at mission control tell the astronauts that there is a defect with the space suits I think, so they would die if they went on this mission and into space. But, it is too late to cancel the trip because of political issues and the space program would take a serious blow and may get canceled, yada, yada, yada. So they decide to fake the trip as far as having actual astronauts on the rocket. They decide to send a rocket that can be flown completely by remote from the control center, and fake the part about the astronauts being on board and landing. The three astronauts are convinced to be a part of this lie and are sent to a special set that looks like the martian landscape where the rocket is going to be landed via remotely by the control center. The set is in a secret hanger somewhere, and with alot of fancy camera equipment and computers, they make it look real. They use like slow motion and stuff to make it look like the guys were actually on Mars with the lighter atmosphere and so on. Anyway, everything goes great with the remote rocket as it takes off from Earth, soars out to Mars and lands. Then the guys back on Earth on the set are seen coming down the ladder of the rocket and stepping down onto the Mars turf. Then they walked around and all this was broadcast on national television, like they did with the moon miisions earlier. It works, as everyone thinks that these astronauts are actually on Mars. However, during the remote flight back from Mars, something happens to the rocket and it explods as it enters the Earths atmosphere, and all on national TV.<BR>So now the government has a real problem. The astronauts are really on Earth and haven't died, even though it looks like it on TV.<BR>So how does the governement decide to handle this little problem? They decide to get rid of all the evidence of this fake mission.<BR>That means that they have to kill these three astronauts, as they aren't suppose to be alive. As far as everyone on Earth thinks, they died during re-entry.<BR>The chase is on as the three astronauts try break out and make it back to civilation and spill the beans before they are taken out.<P>The name of the movie?<P>Capricorn One<P>The name of that "actor"? OJ Simpson<P>Steve<P>------------------<BR>                        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero9supersig_1.jpg">                      <BR>http://www.kelleyfamilyfieros.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||9
Z||000034||Ken Wittlief||05-26-2001||01:36 AM||||there is one part of apollo 11 that I do think was faked. When Buzz climbed down the ladder for the first time, they had a live camera on him, with a pretty good side shot of the lander and him climbing down the ladder.<P>  It would of added a lot of weight to put a self deploying camera on the side of the lander, and have it extend way out like that, just to capture his first decent down the ladder. <P>  I think what really happened is Buzz went out there and set the camera up on a tripod, that they used for all the other camera shots, brushed his footprints away, when back inside, they turned the camera on, and then he climbed down the ladder again, for the 'first' step on the moon.<P>  just like when I was a kid and we came down the stairs on Christmas morning, and dad had the movie camera on to capture the look on our faces. "wait, I have to wind the camera, go back upstairs and come down again"<P>  Christmas 1961, Take Two! Annnnnnnnd ACTION!||||reg||1
Z||000035||Formula88||05-26-2001||03:20 PM||||Well, speaking as a NASA-alumni:<P>The radiation belts:  No we didn't shield them from it completely.  Some shielding, coupled with the fact that they punched through the belt quickly rather than sitting there waiting for their eyes to boil, limited their exposure.<P>No stars in the lunar photos:  Anyone ever take a picture on earth?  Ever heard of a thing called exposure?  When setting the exposure for the bright reflections on the lunar surface, the stars were lost because they were so much dimmer.<P>There was recently a show on Discovery talking about how it was faked, and dispelled those arguments.  <P>BTW, if you're still not convinced - go the Kennedy Space Center and watch a launch.  No, that doesn't prove we landed on the moon, but you'll be hard pressed to explain that hoax when you can witness first hand all that NASA is capable of.  Things work differently at NASA because they think outside of the box by design.  We start with something that can't be done, and then figure out how to do it.  <P>Why did we stop going?  Diminishing returns.  We had done enough of the science to not make it worth the expense to go back solely for research.  Lunar mining, colonization, larger missions weren't funded - so there was no compelling reason to return.  Now with the International Space Station, it's time we stopped playing in our own backyard and ventured forth again into that great unknown.  <P>"If the same amount of energy went into the space program that went into studying the female breast, we would now be operating hot dog stands on Mars."||||reg||1
Z||000036||Cliff Pennock||05-26-2001||05:43 PM||||I'm absolutely 100% convinced we went to the moon. Look at it this way: if the moon landing was faked, then obviously <B>all</B> Apollo missions were faked for the same reasons.<P>Really, I haven't seen or heared one single thing that made me even consider otherwise. All those so called pro-hoax <I>evidence</I> are really incredibly easy to counter. In fact, most of them actually proof that we've been there (either that, or the fakers must have had an austounding eye for detail). No stars in the pictures? If there were, <B>then</B> I would consider it a fake (because it's simply would not be possible to see stars). Perfect in-focus pictures? Of course. Any photographer can actually make perfect pictures without using the view-finder (next time there's some kind of celebrity program on tv, watch the photographers. Most of them shoot pictures while holding their camera above their heads). Crosshairs behind objects on photos? Of course. It's called "bleeding" and is a well known effect when parts of an image are overexposed. The Van Allen Belt? Yes, that was a risk they were taking since they had no idea if the ship and the astronauts' suits would be enough protection. Fortunately it was. But hey, taking risks is what the government does best. They also took a risk when they triggered the first A-bomb since they couldn't figure out if the chain-reaction would or wouldn't blow our atmosphere to kingdom come.<P>And if you look at the moon footage, it just <B>feels</B> right. Even though none of us has ever been to the moon, we are somehow able to distinguish fake from real. Even with today's special effects and CGI, if you look at a moon-scene in a movie, it just doesn't feel right. If I remember correctly, one of the austronauts demonstrated on film that in a vacuum, a feather and a steel ball will fall down at the same speed. No way they could have faked that at that time.||||reg||1
Z||000037||JSocha||05-26-2001||06:21 PM||||You all know my feelings on this topic.<P>However, I believe the astranots should have made a bigger impression with something that would stand out and be able to be seen from Earth with the naked eye other then a little flag and pole.<P>Like a big note scratched into the dirt similiar to what a Castaway might do if stranded on a deserted island with the word "HELP" but with humor.<P>Like:  <B>"HI MOM!  Send Cookies!"</B> or <B>"OKay!?  Who Farted?"</B>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Yea, yea, yea...I understand of course it would have taken them awhile to do this, but at least that couldn't be faked and "WE" would know they had been there!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by JSocha (edited 05-26-2001).]||||reg||3
