Z||000052||WampusCat||05-29-2001||12:19 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B>sorry I meant F117 (typo)<BR>F111 was the 'swingwing' med bomber, used in Nam and Lybia called the Raven<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>OK, I know this is really anal/nitpicky, but the General Dynamics F111 was the Aardvark.  The Raven was an electronics warfare variant designated the EF111A.  You can tell the Ravens by the big EW pod in the vertical stabilizer similar to an EA-6B prowler.  <p>[This message has been edited by WampusCat (edited 05-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000053||newbie88||05-31-2001||03:40 PM||||The radiation belts you are refering to are the VAN ALLEN BELTS, which were discovered by Explorer 1, the first US Satellite.  A normal human can take a dose of about 300 RAD.  With the escape velocity being about 11.6 kilometres per second, the astronauts got a dose of about 1 RAD.  Not even detrimental.  FOX has proven over and over again that they will support bad science in order to boost ratings.  We went there.<BR>Newbie<P>P.S. The Roswell Autopsy was fake, although I do believe that something landed in Roswell||||reg||1
